    "done_when": "Three measured failures of the reflex's review recognition in reckon/crew/recovery.py (the in-flight check near _review_in_flight, and the review node composition near :395-420):\n(a) Duplicate: on 2026-09-26 a hand-dispatched re-review-of-harness-home-carries-mcp-servers and the reflex's review-of-harness-home-carries-mcp-servers ran concurrently on the identical review-store paths, because recognition keyed on node id.\n(b) Missed: the reflex skipped a review for a resumed run that had moved to a new head, reported twice on git-shim-checks-the-resolved-repo, plausibly from a once-per-run key.\n(c) Brief: the composed review done-when does not ask for the added-failures-by-id count that reckon/crew/review.py now computes (merged at d8c0a05c).\nFirst confirm (a) and (b) reproduce at base in a synthesised temporary project with live pointers.\nDone when:\n- a live review of run R at head H, under any node id, suppresses the reflex for (R, H);\n- a stored review record for (R, H) suppresses it too;\n- a run resumed to a new head H2 with no review at H2 gets exactly one reflex review;\n- the composed done-when names the added-failures-by-id count from the reviewed run's own base and head gate logs.\nAssert through the reflex entry point, not a helper. Leave the obligations hook files alone; another coordinator owns them. Tests run under a temporary config home with the real config home asserted untouched. At least one added assertion fails at the dispatch base. Measured files: tests/test_reflex_keys_on_reviewed_run_and_head.py (new) plus the existing reflex and recovery tests your change reaches, named in the manifest, in ONE invocation, with zero added failures against base. If they carry failures that also fail at base, also capture an exit-0 run over the ids that pass at base, with command and EXIT, as the promotion gate. Report ruff findings on the staged paths against the count at base.",
